    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5d2f584_5c892bf7",
        "filename": "rialto/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 68,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T10:14:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The point that Jiyong and I are trying to get across is that, even though there might only ever be one payload that has those distinct capabilities, and even if those capabilities end up always being given to the same VM, there\u0027s no need to make pvmfw unnecessarily more complex with this information. Having a set of one-to-one mappings between IDs and operations is much easier, clearer, and cleaner to deal with than one-to-many, in particular when we start combining them.\n\nTo make this less theoretical, could you list what pvmfw would need to perform for the service VM that it wouldn\u0027t for Microdroid? I\u0027m aware of the need to pass the RPMB key but not sure what \"`remote_attest`\" would involve.",
      "parentUuid": "25b84564_8e41bfd1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "9dabbe3d54a577a8b61690da5aefc42e63d50768",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58818c61_eec83491",
        "filename": "rialto/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 68,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T11:04:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For remote attestation, we mostly want to add a marker in the DICE chain[1] in pvmfw. \n[1] http://doc/1SetVcA-i6MyyWpgXc1fULkklDAUsOQBVYpYJfspfsF8#heading\u003dh.76x4zw6dnnm\n\n---\nThe service VM is a special type of baremetal VM that doesn\u0027t have Microdroid. We aim to make it a singleton to service various needs such as RPMB and remote attestation. Using multiple capabilities in the latest PS actually makes it appear like a usual Microdroid VM with additional capabilities.\n\nHaving only the service_vm capability makes it easier for pvmfw. pvmfw simply needs to identify the service_vm and perform operations A, B, and C. Although with multiple tags, pvmfw can distinguish between operations like cap_a for A, cap_b for B, etc., it\u0027s artificial and misleading. It implies that we sometimes perform A or B, while in reality, all three operations (A, B, and C) are performed together or not at all.\n\nIt\u0027s unclear why pvmfw needs to know the internal details of the service VM. From a coding perspective, more tags also create more scenarios to handle for both pvmfw and the client code, such as when cap_a is on, but cap_b and cap_c are missing.",
      "parentUuid": "c5d2f584_5c892bf7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "9dabbe3d54a577a8b61690da5aefc42e63d50768",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
