      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T11:24:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems almost resolved, so just +1 to what Pierre and Jiyong are saying. Fine-grained caps decouple pvmfw from the VM and give us (and partners) the flexibility to reuse them in other scenarios, eg. if we decide to split RPMB into its own VM. Obviously we should be careful to avoid conflicts between them, but keep them as small exclusions from various aspects of pvmfw default flow. We already do that with things like debug policy anyway...",
      "parentUuid": "58818c61_eec83491",
